# Add support for ARM64 on macOS
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12716 state=merged
# This MR adds support for ARM64 Wine on macOS.

Two new configure options are added: `--enable-codesign-identity` and `--enable-provisioning-profile`.
A restricted entitlement is needed to run Wine, and an Apple developer account is needed to obtain a signing certificate and provisioning profile that must be passed to `configure`. I've created a wiki page (still something of a work-in-progress) outlining the steps: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/wikis/MacOS-Building/ARM64-Provisioning-Profiles. I'll also be adding instructions to https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/wikis/MacOS-Building soon.

Also, note that macOS 27 is required. Although the needed APIs are present in macOS 26.5, the position of the dyld shared cache prevents PAGEZERO from reserving the entire low 8GB. This can prevent particularly large, non-relocatable EXEs from loading. On macOS 27, PAGEZERO can reserve the entire low 8GB and the dyld shared cache loads elsewhere.
